shown.message:
I pushed the bibliography to `paper-repo` `dev` as `refs/refs.bib` and `refs/README.md`, and closed `idea-repo`#5.

It has 37 entries: the prior-work entries from `positioning/`, plus the datasets, software and metrics the paper must cite (folktables, UCI German Credit, Pima, Give Me Some Credit, Arrhythmia, shap, TreeSHAP, XGBoost, LightGBM, scikit-learn, Nogueira, RBO). It builds with BibTeX, with two harmless warnings (Ghorbani has both volume and number; the Kolpaczki antithetic top-k entry has no publisher).

- **Confirmed against Crossref, OpenAlex or DataCite:**
  - the authors, venue and pages for the regression-adjusted Monte Carlo paper (Witter, Liu, Musco);
  - Dong & Rudin;
  - the Kolpaczki antithetic top-k paper, whose key is now `kolpaczki2025antithetic`;
  - the Kolpaczki top-k bandits paper, which turned out to be an LMU repository item, so it is now `@misc`;
  - XGBoost, the German Credit and Arrhythmia dataset records, and the volume, issue and pages of the other journal entries.
- **Still entered from memory:** LightGBM, scikit-learn, Pima and the Arrhythmia co-authors. Their `note` fields say so, and `paper-repo` should cite only the ones the study actually uses.

I also added a pointer to `refs/refs.bib` in `positioning/README.md` and pushed a copy of `refs/` to `idea-repo` `main`. `idea-repo`#2 stays open.
